  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        40,
        -510
      ],
      "size": [
        1560,
        650
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 0,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## LTX 2.5 CrossView Warp \u2014 Balanced\n\n1. Install WeeTodd Nodes and restart ComfyUI.\n2. Place the LTX 2.5 split components under `ComfyUI/models/` or a shared root from `extra_model_paths.yaml`.\n3. Download CrossView Warp v2 and Ingredients into `ComfyUI/models/loras/` (subfolders are supported).\n4. Download Video Depth Anything Small and run the README conversion command once.\n5. Select a 121-frame source movie. The workflow center-crops it to 768\u00d7512 before depth and warp preprocessing. Leave the video selector empty when sharing this workflow.\n6. Choose a source frame that clearly shows the people and scene. The selected frame is previewed and sent through the Ingredients reference IC-LoRA.\n7. The workflow connects the source movie's audio to `publication_audio`, preserving it during final muxing instead of publishing generated audio.\n8. Set a camera-path frame, use **Mode: place camera** to position it, and click **Add / Update**. Repeat for each keyframe. The green curve follows the selected interpolation; its small dots mark equal times so easing is visible. Switch to **Mode: rotate view**, or Shift/right-drag, to inspect every side without changing camera poses. Drag for yaw/pitch and Option-drag for roll.\n9. Inspect the saved moving magenta-hole warp preview before generation. This is the complete per-frame guide, not one middle frame.\n10. In the Ingredients guide, keep `crossview` and replace the bracketed dialogue placeholder with the source speech verbatim. This gives sampling the linguistic cue needed for closer mouth motion.\n11. Keep the prompt `crossview` for the first validation. Describe newly revealed content when distance exceeds 1.0.\n12. Queue the workflow after **LTX 2.5 Preflight** succeeds. The Generate node publishes the final regenerated video with the original soundtrack.\n\nThe model stack applies CrossView first and Ingredients second. The CrossView guide appends two references in the trained order: warp first, source second. Keep both guide strengths at 1.0. Adapter strength 1.3 is recommended for people; use 1.0\u20131.15 for vehicles and rigid objects. Start within \u00b145\u00b0 azimuth and \u221220\u00b0 to +30\u00b0 elevation. Distance control is weak in v2. The selected paged transformer automatically enables low-RAM streaming and the compatible reference_fp32 feed-forward path; users do not need to coordinate those controls manually.\n\n### Downloads\n\n- [LTX 2.5 model components](https://huggingface.co/Lightricks/LTX-2.5)\n- [CrossView Warp v2 IC-LoRA](https://huggingface.co/Cseti/LTX2.3-22B_IC-LoRA-CrossView-Warp_v2)\n- [Ingredients IC-LoRA](https://huggingface.co/Lightricks/LTX-2.3-22b-IC-LoRA-Ingredients)\n- [Video Depth Anything Small](https://huggingface.co/depth-anything/Video-Depth-Anything-Small)\n\n### One-time MLX depth conversion\n\n`$COMFYUI_ROOT/.venv/bin/python $COMFYUI_ROOT/custom_nodes/WeeTodd-Nodes/scripts/convert_video_depth_anything_mlx.py $COMFYUI_ROOT/models/annotators/video_depth_anything/video_depth_anything_vits.pth $COMFYUI_ROOT/models/annotators/video_depth_anything/video_depth_anything_vits_mlx.safetensors`\n\n### Audio and lip-sync\n\nThe untouched source audio is muxed after generation, so it remains clean. It is not used as audio-reference conditioning because CrossView plus Ingredients already uses the two validated IC-LoRA task slots and the current generator rejects the unvalidated video-reference + audio-reference LipDub topology. For speaking clips, paste the source dialogue verbatim into the Ingredients guide. This improves mouth intent but is not sample-exact lip-sync."
      ],
      "title": "Setup and model downloads",
      "color": "#243447",
      "bgcolor": "#15202b"
    },
